{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-e3fd89a1-513b-4f47-b7dc-3ef2f5c7d793","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-86fd75ea45a9b7c3","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-upoq9jg3/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md","content":"# AMD Instinct validation campaign for vLLM ROCm serving parity\n\n## Description\n\nRuns a validation campaign on physical AMD Instinct accelerators to establish\nfunctional and performance parity data for vLLM serving of the platform's supported\nmodel set, and produces the go/no-go scope that determines which models the\nproductized ROCm serving runtime will support. This resolves the strategy's core\nunknown — the platform ships only CUDA runtime builds and has no first-hand ROCm\nparity data for its supported models.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define the campaign protocol: enumerate the supported model set, define per-model\n  functional pass/fail criteria, and define the performance parity measurement\n  methodology (throughput and latency on AMD Instinct versus the productized CUDA\n  baseline).\n- Establish the hardware access arrangement required to execute the campaign —\n  procurement of dedicated AMD Instinct nodes or a partner-lab engagement (the\n  strategy flags this access as unresolved).\n- Execute the campaign: serve each supported model with vLLM ROCm builds on AMD\n  Instinct hardware, collecting functional results and performance measurements.\n- Produce the validation report: per-model functional and performance results, a\n  go/no-go recommendation stating the cleared model scope for productization, and\n  root-cause notes for models that fail or underperform.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The validation report covers every model in the supported model set, recording a\n  functional pass/fail result and performance measurements against the CUDA baseline\n  for each model.\n- The report states