ge compatible with the platform\n  release, and the pinning is recorded.\n- Existing CUDA-based runtime images and ServingRuntime definitions are unaffected\n  (no regression to the currently supported serving paths).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0): a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime productized for the models the\n  validation campaign clears.\n\n## Risks and Notes\n\n- Upstream ROCm image release cadence is controlled by AMD and may not align with\n  the platform release trains; the mitigation is pinning whichever released upstream\n  image is compatible, and re-pinning per release. This timing risk is externally\n  controlled and cannot be compressed.\n- The model scope of this epic is determined by the validation campaign outcome; a\n  partial pass rescopes the epic to the cleared subset, and a full no-go descopes\n  the productization work entirely.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":52718,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9164f842ed079c3c","agent_id":"aa58d3ccd41d49591","session_id":"cfc5c49c-9bde-4a05-b3d1-1a240781a747","uuid":"96ee6f0c-eb61-4a22-bb62-f47db5c4e9d7","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:27:46.375Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020 into epics"}
