DIA-based PyTorchJob behavior is unaffected.\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- HLR-3 (P1): PyTorch training on ROCm supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs —\n57\t  the job-execution half; queue admission and amd.com/gpu quota handling are covered\n58\t  by the Kueue quota work on the Distributed Workloads component.\n59\t\n60\t## Risks and Notes\n61\t\n62\t- Functional validation requires physical AMD Instinct hardware, which is not yet\n63\t  in the CI fleet; access is being arranged through the serving validation\n64\t  campaign's hardware work and remains a shared availability risk.\n65\t- PyTorch ROCm training images depend on upstream PyTorch/AMD ROCm releases whose\n66\t  cadence is externally controlled.\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88146ce14146901d","agent_id":"ab45f5054681bada7","session_id":"cfc5c49c-9bde-4a05-b3d1-1a240781a747","uuid":"8a924cf8-f4b6-4a32-b909-9d13da5e9a01","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:30:17.151Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b274ba900334b55","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
