{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-807d243cd01c6230","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E004\n3\ttitle: Kueue quota handling for AMD GPU (amd.com/gpu) resources\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Kueue quota handling for AMD GPU (amd.com/gpu) resources\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tExtends the Distributed Workloads queueing layer so that workloads requesting AMD\n34\tGPU resources (`amd.com/gpu`) are admitted through Kueue with correct quota\n35\thandling, providing the admission path for ROCm training jobs. This covers the\n36\tqueueing and quota half of ROCm training support; PyTorchJob execution itself is\n37\thandled by the Training Operator work.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Support `amd.com/gpu` in the Kueue quota model: ClusterQueue/LocalQueue resource\n42\t  flavors covering AMD GPU resources so workloads requesting them are admitted\n43\t  under quota with all-or-nothing (gang) admission semantics.\n44\t- Validate quota accounting and admission for multi-GPU PyTorchJob workloads\n45\t  requesting `amd.com/gpu`, including enforcement of quota limits.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- Workloads requesting `amd.com/gpu` are admitted through Kueue quota\n50\t  (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue) and run to completion, including multi-GPU PyTorchJob\n51\t  topologies.\n52\t- Quota limits on `amd.com/gpu` are enforced: a workload whose request exceeds its\n53\t  queue's quota remains pending rather than being partially admitted.\n54\t- Existing NVIDIA GPU (`nvidia.com/gpu`) quota handling and queue behavior are\n55\t  unaffected.\n56\t\n57\t## HLR Traceability\n58\t\n59\t- HLR-3 (P1): PyTorch training on ROCm for jobs admitted through Kueue with\n60\t  amd.com/gpu quota handling — the queue-admission and quota half.\n61\t\n62\t## Risks and Notes\n63\t\n64\t- End-to-end admission validation on real hardware benefits from AMD Instinct node\n65\t  access (shared availability risk with the rest of the strategy); admission and\n66\t  quota semantics can otherwise be exercised with fake/simulated resource flavors.\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88146ce14146901d","agent_id":"ab45f5054681bada7","session_id":"cfc5c49c-9bde-4a05-b3d1-1a240781a747","uuid":"f461b084-b5db-403d-9dba-c55714a36305","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:30:17.783Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-807d243cd01c6230","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
