e's scope.\n55\t- Using ROCm training: submitting single- and multi-GPU PyTorchJobs and requesting\n56\t  `amd.com/gpu` quota through the platform's queueing layer.\n57\t- Scope boundaries carried from the strategy: non-AMD accelerator families and AMD\n58\t  GPU sharing/partitioning are not supported.\n59\t\n60\t## Acceptance Criteria\n61\t\n62\t- Published documentation states the supported AMD hardware, driver prerequisites,\n63\t  and the validated model list, consistent with the validation campaign results and\n64\t  the productized ROCm serving runtime and training support.\n65\t- The content is technically reviewed against the implementations by the owning\n66\t  engineering teams before publication.\n67\t- The documentation is available in the platform release in which the ROCm support\n68\t  ships.\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\t- HLR-4 (P2): documentation stating supported AMD hardware, driver prerequisites,\n73\t  and the validated model list.\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88146ce14146901d","agent_id":"ab45f5054681bada7","session_id":"cfc5c49c-9bde-4a05-b3d1-1a240781a747","uuid":"2a7e6a18-e353-4de1-be34-85bc2af48098","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:30:18.362Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a39b1280ff720314","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
